|}France achieved its most successful World Championships in the tournament's history, winning two gold medals. Alex Lanier became the first French player to win a men's singles world title, while Thom Gicquel and Delphine Delrue won France's first mixed doubles world championship.<ref>{{Cite news |date=August 23, 2026 |title=Lanier crushes Naraoka to become first Frenchman to win singles world title |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/lanier-crushes-naraoka-become-first-frenchman-win-singles-world-title-2026-08-23/ |access-date=August 28, 2026 |work=Reuters}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-08-23 |title='No one will be waiting at the airport': Inside France's historic double gold at the World Championships |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/badminton/no-one-will-be-waiting-at-the-airport-inside-frances-historic-double-gold-at-the-world-championships/articleshow/133442158.cms |access-date=2026-08-28 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257}}</ref>

